        "original_id": "df7eadf3-5d8d-547c-9649-716d8519e556",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Joy Formidable, Sixpence None the Richer\n- People: Leigh Nash\n- Music releases: A Heavy Abacus, The Big Roar, Wishing for This\n- Places: North Wales, London, England, New Braunfels, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n\nFacts:\n- The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band formed in 2007 in North Wales and now based in London, England.\n- Sixpence None the Richer, also known as Sixpence, is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, and later settled in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- \"A Heavy Abacus\" is the fifth and final single from The Joy Formidable's debut album \"The Big Roar,\" and it was released in July 2011.\n- \"Wishing for This\" is a Christmas EP by Leigh Nash, who is a member of Sixpence None the Richer.",
